# Day 27

## Experiment Title

Managing Docker Compose Containers and Services


## Objective

To learn how to manage and monitor containers and services created using Docker Compose.


## Theory

Docker Compose provides commands to start, stop, restart, and monitor multiple containers together. It helps users manage application services efficiently from a single interface.

Using Docker Compose, users can inspect running containers, view logs, restart services, and remove unused resources. Proper container management improves application maintenance and troubleshooting.


## Requirements

Docker Desktop

Docker Compose

Windows Operating System


## Procedure

Open Docker Desktop and verify that Docker services are running.

Start the Docker Compose application.

View the list of running containers and active services.

Monitor container logs and application activity.

Restart selected services and observe the changes.

Stop and remove the Docker Compose application after completion.


## Output

Docker Compose services were successfully managed and monitored.

Container logs and service information were displayed correctly.

Application services were restarted and controlled successfully.


## Result

Successfully learned how to manage and monitor Docker Compose containers and services.
